      "desc": "On-die Network-on-Chip: a 2D mesh of routers, one per Tensix tile, that moves data between Tensix cores, the GDDR6 controllers and the Ethernet cores. Two independent NoC planes (NoC0/NoC1) run in opposite directions to avoid deadlock. This mesh is the same fabric philosophy that continues off-die over Ethernet — on-die and chip-to-chip transfers use the same addressing model.",
