  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights and activations sit in GDDR6 packages next to each ASIC — Wormhole has no on-package HBM.",
      "focus": [
        "gddr6-die0",
        "gddr6-die1"
      ],
      "dot": "gddr6-die0",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. A GDDR6 controller on the die reads the tile and hands it to the on-die NoC mesh.",
      "focus": [
        "die0",
        "noc-die0"
      ],
      "dot": "noc-die0",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. If the tile lives on the other ASIC's GDDR6, it crosses the Warp 100 bridge over two of the 16 on-die Ethernet cores — the same fabric used for chip-to-chip scale-out, not a dedicated interconnect.",
      "focus": [
        "ethernet-die0",
        "ethernet-die1"
      ],
      "dot": "ethernet-die0",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. The NoC routes the tile to a specific Tensix core and its 1.5 MB L1 SRAM.",
      "focus": [
        "tensix-die0"
      ],
      "dot": "tensix-die0",
      "drill": "tensix-detail",
      "stage": "l1"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Two of the core's 5 RISC-Vs (brisc/ncrisc) move the tile between the NoC and L1; a third (trisc0) kicks off the Unpacker to expand it into working layout.",
      "focus": [
        "riscv-noc0",
        "riscv-noc1",
        "riscv-trisc0",
        "unpack-unit"
      ],
      "dot": "unpack-unit",
      "drill": "tensix-detail",
      "stage": "unpack"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. trisc1 drives the FPU: the matrix engine multiplies 32×32 tiles (BF16/TF32, or BFP8 block-floating-point for FP8-class throughput).",
      "focus": [
        "riscv-trisc1",
        "fpu-matrix-engine"
      ],
      "dot": "fpu-matrix-engine",
      "drill": "tensix-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. The SFPU vector engine applies elementwise ops — bias, activation, requantization — on the FPU's output.",
      "focus": [
        "sfpu-vector-engine"
      ],
      "dot": "sfpu-vector-engine",
      "drill": "tensix-detail",
      "stage": "sfpu"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. trisc2 drives the Packer, recompressing the result back into L1.",
      "focus": [
        "riscv-trisc2",
        "pack-unit"
      ],
      "dot": "pack-unit",
      "drill": "tensix-detail",
      "stage": "pack"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. ncrisc pushes the result back onto the NoC — to a neighboring Tensix core for the next layer, or out toward GDDR6/Ethernet.",
      "focus": [
        "riscv-noc1"
      ],
      "dot": "riscv-noc1",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
